### Restate Workflow Interpreter — demo requests (IntelliJ HTTP Client)
### Base URL = the ingress of a locally running restate-server.
@host = http://localhost:8080

### 1) Define the "demo" workflow (store its JSON representation).
### Expressions (branch `condition`, llm `prompt`, parallel `items`) are jq programs
### over { results, input, item, index }.
POST {{host}}/WorkflowDefinition/demo/set
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "demo",
  "steps": [
    { "id": "todo", "type": "http", "method": "GET", "url": "https://jsonplaceholder.typicode.com/todos/1" },
    { "id": "wait", "type": "sleep", "durationMillis": 1000 },
    { "id": "route", "type": "branch", "branches": [
      { "condition": ".results.todo.body.completed == true", "steps": [ { "id": "quick", "type": "sleep", "durationMillis": 500 } ] }
    ], "default": [ { "id": "review", "type": "sleep", "durationMillis": 1500 } ] },
    { "id": "analysis", "type": "llm", "model": "gpt-4o-mini",
      "prompt": "\"Classify this TODO and suggest three tags. Title: \" + .results.todo.body.title",
      "schema": { "type": "object", "properties": {
        "sentiment": { "type": "string", "enum": ["positive", "neutral", "negative"] },
        "tags": { "type": "array", "items": { "type": "string" } }
      }, "required": ["sentiment", "tags"], "additionalProperties": false } },
    { "id": "fanout", "type": "parallel", "items": "[.results.todo.body.userId, .results.todo.body.id]", "body": [
      { "id": "post", "type": "http", "method": "GET", "url": "https://jsonplaceholder.typicode.com/posts/1" }
    ] }
  ]
}

### 2) Read the stored definition back
POST {{host}}/WorkflowDefinition/demo/get
Accept: application/json

### 3) Start it now — the request body is the starting `input`. Returns { "invocationId": "..." }
POST {{host}}/WorkflowDefinition/demo/start
Content-Type: application/json

{ "greeting": "Hello" }

> {%
    client.global.set("invocationId", response.body.invocationId);
    client.log("started invocation " + response.body.invocationId);
%}

### 4) Poll the invocation's status by id
GET {{host}}/restate/invocation/{{invocationId}}/status
Accept: application/json

### 5) Attach to the invocation — blocks until it completes, returns the workflow result
GET {{host}}/restate/invocation/{{invocationId}}/attach
Accept: application/json

### 5b) Stream progress: long-poll the per-step event log. Repeat this request with
### the returned `nextIndex` as `afterIndex` to keep streaming until $workflow completes.
POST {{host}}/WorkflowEvents/{{invocationId}}/watch
Content-Type: application/json

{ "afterIndex": 0, "timeoutSeconds": 30 }

### 5c) Or read the whole progress log at once
POST {{host}}/WorkflowEvents/{{invocationId}}/list
Accept: application/json

### 6) Schedule it to run 10 seconds in the future, with its own input
POST {{host}}/WorkflowDefinition/demo/schedule
Content-Type: application/json

{ "delayMillis": 10000, "input": { "greeting": "Later" } }

> {% client.global.set("scheduledId", response.body.invocationId); %}

### 7) Poll the scheduled invocation (PENDING until the delay elapses, then runs)
GET {{host}}/restate/invocation/{{scheduledId}}/status
Accept: application/json

### 8) List every invocation id started from this definition
POST {{host}}/WorkflowDefinition/demo/invocations
Accept: application/json

###############################################################################
# LLM demo: "blog-ideas" — an LLM-driven pipeline. Needs OPENAI_API_KEY set on
# the running service (export it or put it in a .env file).
###############################################################################

### 9) Define the "blog-ideas" workflow
POST {{host}}/WorkflowDefinition/blog-ideas/set
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "blog-ideas",
  "steps": [
    { "id": "ideas", "type": "llm", "model": "gpt-4o-mini", "system": "You are a punchy content strategist.",
      "prompt": "\"Give me 3 blog post ideas about: \" + .input.topic",
      "schema": { "type": "object", "properties": { "ideas": { "type": "array", "items": { "type": "string" } } }, "required": ["ideas"], "additionalProperties": false } },
    { "id": "drafts", "type": "parallel", "items": ".results.ideas.ideas[]", "body": [
      { "id": "draft", "type": "llm", "model": "gpt-4o-mini",
        "prompt": "\"Blog idea: \" + .item + \". Topic: \" + .input.topic + \". Write a catchy title, a 3-bullet outline, and a tweet.\"",
        "schema": { "type": "object", "properties": { "title": { "type": "string" }, "outline": { "type": "array", "items": { "type": "string" } }, "tweet": { "type": "string" } }, "required": ["title", "outline", "tweet"], "additionalProperties": false } }
    ] }
  ]
}

### 10) Start it with a topic (the request body is the input). Returns { invocationId }
POST {{host}}/WorkflowDefinition/blog-ideas/start
Content-Type: application/json

{ "topic": "durable execution" }

> {% client.global.set("llmInvocationId", response.body.invocationId); %}

### 11) Attach for the result — several LLM calls, so give it a few seconds
GET {{host}}/restate/invocation/{{llmInvocationId}}/attach
Accept: application/json
